I follow Nina's route.
It is Saturday morning.
Now I walk down the main street.
First I just walk straight ahead.
The street is very busy.
On the way I look at three yellow bicycles.
The bicycles ride quickly past me.
After that I walk further ahead.
Then I come to a large park.
Suddenly I remember Nina's words.
"Turn left at the park," she says.
Here I turn left.
A little later I see an open door.
It is a small bakery.
There is a lovely smell of fresh coffee.
I love warm bread.
Today the city is lovely.
Afterwards I walk on towards the water.
